<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isci> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "International Standard Collection Identifier (ISCI) is a variable-length identifier standardized by ISO 27730 <https://www.iso.org/standard/44293.html> for identifying collections held by libraries, archives, museums, and other memory institutions. It consists of two parts: the identifier for the assigning organization (an ISIL) enclosed in square brackets, followed by a local collection identifier string (e.g., [FR-751041001]Casadesus1)."@en .
