<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/nli> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Natural Location Identifier (NLI) <https://eccma.org/enli-eccma-natural-location-identifier/> is a 14- or 15-character alphanumeric string standardized by ISO 8000-118 <https://www.iso.org/standard/85428.html> that uniquely identifies a three-dimensional geographic point location. The identifier is generated from geodetic coordinates and elevation data. For electronic storage, the ISO.NLI: prefix shall be retained (e.g., ISO.NLI:41TS8M-A8ELTQ-H2)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/actionLocation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The location of an action is defined by the actionLocation. Action locations help define and validate a specific action."@en .
