<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Service/serviceHostingCountry> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Specifies a country or territory where a software service is located.\nThis includes indirect locations (e.g., where the data may be hosted).\n\nThe string shall be in the ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 <https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:3166:-1> three-letter format.\nSee the ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 Wikipedia page <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-3> for more information."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/attend> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType> .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Relationship> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape> .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Build/parameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "parameter is a key-value of a build parameter and its value that\nwas provided to the builder for a build instance, according to the buildType.\n\nThis is different from the environment property in that\nthe key and value are provided as command line arguments or\na configuration file to the builder."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/name> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "This field identifies the name of an Element as designated by the creator.\n\nThe name of an Element is an important convention and easier to refer to than\nthe URI."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/NoAssertionElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An Individual Value for Element representing a set of Elements of unknown\nidentity or cardinality (number)."@en .
